course: dictionary
lesson: 7086
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, meaning the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Payback has two main meanings: revenge, and money paid back.
explain: «Revenge usually makes a fight bigger, so tell a teacher instead of planning payback.» The clues are the fight and the planning. Here payback means getting even with someone for something they did to you.
explain: In money and maths, payback is different. If the clues are savings, costs or pounds, payback means how long it takes to earn back the money you spent. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
fact: Payback means revenge: doing something bad to someone because they did something bad to you.
fact: Payback also means money paid back, or the time it takes to earn back the money you spent.
fact: Stories often show that revenge is not a good answer, as in «Revenge usually makes a fight bigger».
fact: The phrases «it's payback time» and «as payback for» can be used in either sense, so read the clues around them.
fact: A good check is to swap in revenge or earning back the money and see which one fits.
exercise: «Revenge usually makes a fight bigger, so tell a teacher instead of planning payback.» What does payback mean here? | A kind of bike lock | *Revenge, getting even with someone | A prize for winning a game | Money paid back to a friend
exercise: Ruby saved for a bike and says the payback time is two years. What does payback mean here? | *The time it takes to earn back the money spent | A type of bike | Doing something bad to someone | A present for a friend
exercise: Which sentence uses payback to mean revenge? | *Sam planned payback on Ali after Ali broke his model | Sam's model won a prize at the fair | Sam's savings will cover the cost of his trip | Sam paid back the £5 he borrowed from his gran
test: Mia said, «I'll get payback on you for that.» What is Mia threatening? | To win a race | To give a present to her friend | *To get even with someone who wronged her | To pay back the money she owes
test: Ben's paper round earns back the cost of his bike in six weeks. What does payback mean here? | Doing something kind for a friend | *The time it takes to earn back the money spent | A kind of bike lock | Revenge on the shop that sold it
exam: Why is telling a teacher better than planning payback? | Payback always means money | *Revenge usually makes a fight bigger | It is the only way to win a game | It costs nothing to do
